ll,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":0.10857182389664384,"_gp_fund_growth":true,"_score_fund_growth":100.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.01613123062642671,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":29.0,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.003340838114605273,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":94.4,"_gate_insider_own":0.02654,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":17.7,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Venture Global, Inc., a liquefied natural gas (LNG) company, engages in the ownership, development, construction, and operation of LNG production facilities and associated infrastructure in the United States, Germany, France, Netherlands, the United Kingdom, and internationally.The company is involved in LNG production, natural gas transportation, and regasification operations, as well as LNG sales and shipping business through LNG tankers. Its LNG projects include Calcasieu, Plaquemines, and CP2 projects. The company was founded in 2013 and is headquartered in Arlington, Virginia. Venture Global, Inc. operates as a subsidiary of Venture Global Partners II, LLC.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Michael A. Sabel | Founder, Executive Co-Chairman of the Board & CEO | Age 57 | Compensation: $39.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $6.9M ranks in the top quartile among Energy peers. Stock-based compensation of $23K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 6\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity).","financial_summary":["Venture Global, Inc. is a large-cap energy business with a $28.8B market cap on $13.8B of annual revenue.","Returns on capital run at 11% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically.","The company is burning through $6.8B of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","Accruals are elevated at -8.1% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 5.2\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and interest coverage runs at 3.5\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 1.6%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 2.7% of the shares, and within its sector the business captures 3.4\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.1) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (83.8% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Carries a 43% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.4348016976437874},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $123.5M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 55/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; durably derated by the market \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Energy peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Energy tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Geopolitical supply shocks \u2014 wars, sanctions, and OPEC decisions create volatility that no hedging programme can fully neutralise.","sev":